lla Glitza, MD, PHD\nPhone: 713.792.2921\nEmail: icglitza@mdanderson.org\n\n### Trial #: NCT07331064\n\nClinical Trials.gov\n\n### Intrathecal Application of PD1 Antibody in Metastatic Solid Tumors With Leptomeningeal Disease\n\n#### Goal of study:\n\nTo determine the safety of intrathecal PD1 antibody (Nivolumab) in metastatic solid tumors with leptomeningeal disease.\n\n#### Who this is for:\n\n  * People 18 years and older\n  * Patients with LMD from a solid tumor\n\n#### Contact:\n\n  * Ghazaleh Tabatabai, Prof.Dr.\nPhone: +49 (0) 7071 – 2985018\nEmail:ghazaleh.tabatabai@uni-tuebingen.de\n\n## NOT YET RECRUITING as of September 2026\n\n### Trial #: NCT07178938\n\nLocations:\n\n  * Spain\n\nClinical Trials.gov\n\n### Platform Trial Assessing Uptake, Safety and Efficacy of Theranostic Agents in HER2+ Breast Cancer Patients With Active Brain Metastases (THERANOVA)\n\n#### This study is not yet recruiting participants.\n\n#### Goal of study:\n\nThis trial will evaluate treatment for patients with solid tumors with active brain metastases. Patients will be treated with a theranostic or diagnostic agent. Theranostic agents are targeted radioactive drugs used to identify (diagnose) and to deliver therapy. The main purpose of the study is to analyze the efficacy (to find out how effective a treatment is) of each of the theranostic agents in patients who have solid tumors with active brain metastases. \n\n#### Who this is for:\n\n  * People 18 years and older\n  * Patients with HER2+ breast cancer and active brain metastases or leptomeningeal metastases\n\n#### Contacts:\n\n  * Medsir\n  * Phone: +34 932 214 135\n  * Email: contact.trials@medsir.org\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nA Study of a Selective ERBB2 Inhibitor… | Clinical Trial | OpenTrials (https://opentrials.com/clinical-trials/NCT07361562/a-study-of-a-selective-erbb2-inhibitor-cgt4255-in-patients-with)\nciteturn5search5 [wordlim: 200] Published: 9 months a